<h3 data-start=3D"4023" data-end=3D"4089" class=3D"">3.2 Types de d=C3=A9pe=
ndances : <code data-start=3D"4054" data-end=3D"4068">dependencies</code> e=
t <code data-start=3D"4072" data-end=3D"4089">devDependencies</code></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4091" data-end=3D"4198" class=3D"">Les modules dans Node.j=
s sont class=C3=A9s en deux cat=C3=A9gories principales : <code data-start=
=3D"4162" data-end=3D"4176">dependencies</code> et <code data-start=3D"4180=
" data-end=3D"4197">devDependencies</code>.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4200" data-end=3D"4731">
<li data-start=3D"4200" data-end=3D"4511" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4202" data-end=3D"4370" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
202" data-end=3D"4222"><code data-start=3D"4204" data-end=3D"4218">dependen=
cies</code> :</strong> Ce sont les d=C3=A9pendances n=C3=A9cessaires pour e=
x=C3=A9cuter votre application en production. Ces modules sont utilis=C3=A9=
s =C3=A0 l'int=C3=A9rieur de votre code principal.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4376" data-end=3D"4511" class=3D"">Exemple : Lors de l'uti=
lisation d'Express, ce module sera une <code data-start=3D"4438" data-end=
=3D"4450">dependency</code>, car il est n=C3=A9cessaire pour faire fonction=
ner l'application.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4513" data-end=3D"4731" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4515" data-end=3D"4731" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
515" data-end=3D"4538"><code data-start=3D"4517" data-end=3D"4534">devDepen=
dencies</code> :</strong> Ce sont les d=C3=A9pendances utilis=C3=A9es uniqu=
